cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "isaac-plc-digital-twin: a vendor-neutral PLC to ROS 2 to Isaac Sim digital twin"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Damsarkho"
    given-names: "Nebras"
    alias: "Nebras4u"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nebras4u/isaac-plc-digital-twin"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Open-source digital twin that connects a PLC (simulated with PLCSIM
  Advanced) to a virtual robot in NVIDIA Isaac Sim through ROS 2. A bridge
  reads PLC signals (TCP/JSON, OPC UA or PLCSIM API), a Ruckig-based
  trajectory generator produces smooth setpoints, and a physics executor
  drives the simulated robot and returns its measured state to the PLC.
  Robot, PLC and signal mapping are changed by editing YAML files only.
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - PLC
  - ROS 2
  - Isaac Sim
  - OPC UA
  - virtual commissioning
  - Ruckig
